TI  - Restoration of feeding grounds on former ricefields for wintering waterfowl (Anatidae)
T2  - GIBIER FANE SAUVAGE - GAME AND WILDLIFE, VOL 15 (SPECIAL NUMBER PTS 2 AND 3) 1998
CP  - IUGB XXIIIrd Congress
AB  - An experiment of water management and grazing on 18 former ricefields was conducted in the Camargue, S.France, during five years (1989-1994). The effects of grazing and flooding on the diversity and numbers of ducks were monitored. Seven waterfowl species were observed, mallard, Anas platyrhynchos, and teal, Anas crecca, being the most numerous. During the survey period, their numbers were positively correlated with water levels and negatively correlated with vegetation cover. During rainy winters, all the experimental fields were flooded and the effect of water levels was not significant. No relationship was found between numbers of ducks and food supply (seeds).
